    description: "Repro: `hypergumbo catalog --backend=tree-sitter` -> exit 2 'unrecognized arguments: --backend=tree-sitter'; `hypergumbo catalog --backend tree-sitter`, `hypergumbo --backend=tree-sitter catalog` and `... --backend=tree-sitter --help` all exit 0. test_backend_cli_flag.py only tests `=` before the subcommand. Fix: iterate range(len(argv)) and read argv[idx+1] only when it exists; add a test with `--backend=X` last.\n\nFound by the 2026-10-10 docstring-staleness audit (reviewer + default-REJECT verifier, reproduced). Notebook: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_10102026.md."  # 9257
    fields:  # 9257
      statement: "`--backend` is accepted in any position, in both `--backend X` and `--backend=X` forms (cli.py module docstring)."  # 9257
      root_cause: "main's pre-scan loops `for idx in range(len(argv) - 1)`, so the last token is never examined, even in the `=` form that needs no following token."  # 9257
